 about how we could improve this network. First, let us look at the structure of the network. We have a series of convolutional blocks followed by a linear layer. Each convolutional block consists of two parts: a downsampling operation (using `nn.AvgPool2d`) and a residual connection (using `nn.Conv2d`). The downsampling operation reduces the spatial resolution of the input, while the residual connection allows us to learn more complex features without introducing too much noise into the network. 

Now, let us consider what kind of improvements we could make to this network. One possibility would be to replace the average pooling operations with max pooling operations. This might help the network better capture local features, which could lead to improved performance. Another potential improvement would be to add more layers to each convolutional block. This could allow the network to learn even more complex features, potentially leading to further improvements in performance. Finally, we could also experiment with different activation functions, such as ReLU or LeakyReLU, to see if they provide any benefits over the current sigmoid activation function.

