Parameters are the variables that define the structure of a neural network. These include weights, biases, and activation functions. In other words, they determine how the network will process data. Reducing the number of parameters in a neural network can lead to faster training times and better generalization capabilities. However, reducing the number of parameters too much may result in poor performance due to overfitting.

